        "description": "The printed label fixes the ideal exponential with base 0.25. Every sampled vertex is computed as y=base^x; the shared (0,1) point is hidden, so no answer-bearing marker is added. Source-to-modern limitations: The partial left border strip is regularized to 0.4 units, a modern frame choice rather than an asserted printed abscissa. All complete half-unit grid lines and named bases are retained. Three ideal labelled exponentials replace rough printed strokes without adding markers or answers. Inventory objects are the visible curve strokes and equation label. The hidden vertices referenced by coordinate assertions are renderer construction facts, not extra source point markers.",
